description:
If at all it is possible, then we should define the PLATFORM in .gitlab-ci.yml and then, use this in the dockerfile as: 

 
{code:java}
FROM --platform=${PLATFORM}{code}
 

We should follow the same convention for every other thing that is dependent on the environment, including architecture, target etc etc. Subsequently, our build scripts which are referenced from */scripts* name space should take care of these environment variables to create a relevant build. 

In the CI, we will execute builds for all relevant platforms that are supported.

 

The naming convention followed for docker images *qtbase_${qt_branch_name}_platform*. if there are more things to support, like "target-android", that is appended to the name.

