description:
When running the login-micro-service, the uvicorn server logs should also go to a file so that we are able to check this from there. 

 

[https://stackoverflow.com/questions/60715275/fastapi-logging-to-file] 
{code:java}
I wanted to know how to get FastAPI to log to both a file and the console. Pratik's answer got me most of the way there, but I found that Uvicorn was only logging to the file. At least, this was the case when Uvicorn was integrated into my main script like so:

if __name__ == "__main__":
    cwd = pathlib.Path(__file__).parent.resolve()
    uvicorn.run(app, host="0.0.0.0", port=5000, log_config=f"{cwd}/log.ini")
{code}

The current naming convention is: 
{code:java}
qt_v{qt_branch}_{additional_sdk}_{host_platform}{code}

In squish, the additional SDK is going to be Squish itself. So, we should add that there.

summary_description_acceptance:
Create Squish images in same naming convention as other images $end$ The current naming convention is: 
{code:java}
qt_v{qt_branch}_{additional_sdk}_{host_platform}{code}

In squish, the additional SDK is going to be Squish itself. So, we should add that there.  $acceptance criteria:$

