description:
Currently 3rd party code is used for parsing HTTP headers. Qt seems to have {{QHttpHeaderParser}} class for parsing HTTP responses. Perhaps it could be extended to support HTTP requests and be used instead the 3rd party component.

The used project (https://github.com/nodejs/http-parser) also has this in its README:

{quote}
http-parser is not actively maintained. New projects and projects looking to migrate should consider llhttp.
{quote}

original_description_sprint:
Currently 3rd party code is used for parsing HTTP headers. Qt seems to have {{QHttpHeaderParser}} class for parsing HTTP responses. Perhaps it could be extended to support HTTP requests and be used instead the 3rd party component.

The used project (https://github.com/nodejs/http-parser) also has this in its README:

{quote}
http-parser is not actively maintained. New projects and projects looking to migrate should consider llhttp.
{quote}

description:
Over the past two days, this has come up twice: Unlike with node-based containers, this loop is quadratic with QFlatMap:

{code}
for (auto it = m.begin(), end = m.end(); it != end; /* erasing */)
    if (cond(*m))
        it = m.erase(it);
    else
        ++it;
{code}

A linear, remove_if-like loop is not possible to implement with existing QFlatMap API, so we'd need a remove_if member.

summary_description_acceptance:
Add QFlatMap::remove_if $end$ Over the past two days, this has come up twice: Unlike with node-based containers, this loop is quadratic with QFlatMap:

