description:
QString and QByteArray, unlike all other Qt containers, and unlike std::string, lack the {{erase(it)}} function. Currently, the only option to erase a single character in QString is to use {{erase(it, it + 1)}}, or {{remove(n)}}.

Acceptance criteria: The following tests pass for {{C}} = {{QString}} and {{C}} = {{QByteArray}}:
{code}
C c = "bar";
c.erase(c.begin());
QCOMPARE_EQ(c, "ar");
c.erase(std::prev(c.end()));
QCOMPARE_EQ(c, "a");
{code}

