original_description_sprint:
We should generate code so that users can easily switch on the contained value of a oneof field.

i.e.

{code:cpp}
OneofMessage test = ...;
 switch (test.testOneofCase() /* getter for a oneof field named 'testOneof' */) {
   case OneofMessage::testOneofCase::None:
     // no value
     break;
   case OneofMessage::testOneofCase::testOneofComplexField:
     // the contained 'ComplexField' field is initialized
     ...
   // etc...
 }
{code}

original_summary_description_acceptance_:
Switching on oneof field value $end$ We should generate code so that users can easily switch on the contained value of a oneof field.

i.e.

{code:cpp}
OneofMessage test = ...;
 switch (test.testOneofCase() /* getter for a oneof field named 'testOneof' */) {
   case OneofMessage::testOneofCase::None:
     // no value
     break;
   case OneofMessage::testOneofCase::testOneofComplexField:
     // the contained 'ComplexField' field is initialized
     ...
   // etc...
 }
{code}
 $acceptance criteria:$

description:
This is a spin off from QTBUG-109235, please see there for more info.

I have a hard time deciding whether the toupper() call here:
{code}
qtbase/src/plugins/platforms/windows/qwindowskeymapper.cpp:        a = toupper(a);
{code}
is genuinely supposed to map {{i}} to {{İ} in the Türkiye locale, or whether it shouldn't still be {{I}}. If it is, then the code is wrong, because touppper('i') will likely return 'i', then, since İ isn't representable. So the code is wrong, either way. The question is what the fix should be.

