description:
qdoc should support documenting type aliases:
{code:java}
\typealias QKnxFixedSizeDatapointType 

Alias for QKnxDatapointType.
{code}
qdoc already has the {{\typedef}} command, but this is closely linked - both in term of the command name as in the output - to C++ typedef's, which is just one way of defining type aliases in C++.

