Leverage Conan's built in "conan config install" which can install settings.yml and profiles from git repository or network url.

Setup a new .git repository that contains the settings.yml and profile files for all Qt versions and build targets. Alternatively use existing .git repository.
 * user's responsibility is to call 'conan config install <args>" to install the settings.yml to current work space. Note! This will override the current one.
 * install profile files, up to debate:
 ** Qt Installer can call the "conan config install" for profile files but this is a no-go for offline installers which operate in closed environments
 ** User installs the profile files manually using the same command $acceptance criteria:$

original_description_sprint:
{color:#172b4d}Current conan(.exe) client provided by the Qt Installer contains a patch to support CONAN_USER_HOME next to conan(.exe) out of the box, without playing with environment variables. This enables easier usage of custom conan cache and settings.{color}

{color:#172b4d}This works but the workflow for users is sub-optimal as they may need to use two Conan caches.{color}

 

{color:#172b4d}-> Continue to provide standalone conan(.exe) without modifications.{color}

*{color:#172b4d}Implications:{color}*
 * {color:#172b4d}packages are installed to system conan cache, default under $HOME/.conan{color}
 ** {color:#172b4d}this should be ok as packages are under Qt's namespace{color}
 * {color:#172b4d}settings.yml can not be installed by the Qt Installer, it would be outside Qt installation and would overwrite the users copy in $HOME/.conan/settings.yml{color}
 * {color:#172b4d}profiles can not be installed by Qt Installer outside the Qt installation to $HOME/.conan/profiles{color}

*Solution proposal:*

Leverage Conan's built in "conan config install" which can install settings.yml and profiles from git repository or network url.

Setup a new .git repository that contains the settings.yml and profile files for all Qt versions and build targets. Alternatively use existing .git repository.
 * user's responsibility is to call 'conan config install <args>" to install the settings.yml to current work space. Note! This will override the current one.
 * install profile files, up to debate:
 ** Qt Installer can call the "conan config install" for profile files but this is a no-go for offline installers which operate in closed environments
 ** User installs the profile files manually using the same command

