original_description_sprint:
This task is about doing some refactoring in QtPositioning.

Things to be considered for now:
 * Remove QGeoPositionInfoSourceFactory in favor of QGeoPositionInfoSourceFactoryV2;
 * Rename "org/qtproject/qt5" to "org/qtproject/qt" for android support (see
 https://bugreports.qt.io/browse/QTBUG-86969);
 * Check the module for some deprecated methods, TODO or Qt6 markers;
 * error() signal and error() method clash. Rename the signal to errorOccurred()
 * As a final step - write a porting guide with all API changes.

original_summary_description_acceptance_:
QtPositioning: introduce new API changes $end$ This task is about doing some refactoring in QtPositioning.

Things to be considered for now:
 * Remove QGeoPositionInfoSourceFactory in favor of QGeoPositionInfoSourceFactoryV2;
 * Rename "org/qtproject/qt5" to "org/qtproject/qt" for android support (see
 https://bugreports.qt.io/browse/QTBUG-86969);
 * Check the module for some deprecated methods, TODO or Qt6 markers;
 * error() signal and error() method clash. Rename the signal to errorOccurred()
 * As a final step - write a porting guide with all API changes. $acceptance criteria:$

description:
Many modules that implement some Android feature rely on [QtAndroid::androidSdkVersion()|https://doc.qt.io/qt-5/qtandroid.html#androidSdkVersion] which is used to check the the Android api version to use a correct Java method/API for a given Android version. However, one alternative to that is using QOperatingSystemVersion
{code:java}
if (QOperatingSystemVersion::current() >= QOperatingSystemVersion::AndroidOreo)
    // Do stuff
{code}

