description:
This came up in API review: Instead of separate shape classes (e.g. ParticleShapeSphere3D), combine them all into ParticleShape3D and use type enum instead. Something like this:

shape: ParticleShape3D {
    type: ParticleShape3D.Sphere
    fill: true
}

Also consider adding "Rectangle" type, where only x & y would get random value and z remains 0 (so slightly faster than Cube).

